- **Medium â€” A deleted stored message reappears as pending.** 
[message-cache.ts:54](E:/projects/virtual-office/src/lib/messaging/message-cache.ts:54). Hold HTTP after creation 
commits; let Realtime hide the pending copy; then delete the stored row through another authorized session. Once 
DELETE removes the cached row, its key disappears from `storedKeys`, so the originating tab renders `temp-<key>` as 
sending again; the other tab shows nothing. Pending entries are removed only when HTTP settles. **Smallest fix:** 
retire the pending representation when its stored key is first observed, preserve that resolution across deletion, and 
respect deletion when merging a held response. Add a held-response/deletion E2E regression.

