**Verdict: revision required.** One Medium finding remains.

- **Medium — A deleted stored message reappears as pending.** 
[message-cache.ts:54](E:/projects/virtual-office/src/lib/messaging/message-cache.ts:54). Hold HTTP after creation 
commits; let Realtime hide the pending copy; then delete the stored row through another authorized session. Once 
DELETE removes the cached row, its key disappears from `storedKeys`, so the originating tab renders `temp-<key>` as 
sending again; the other tab shows nothing. Pending entries are removed only when HTTP settles. **Smallest fix:** 
retire the pending representation when its stored key is first observed, preserve that resolution across deletion, and 
respect deletion when merging a held response. Add a held-response/deletion E2E regression.

- **Low — Legacy ChatWindow loses optimistic sends.** 
[useMessages.ts:312](E:/projects/virtual-office/src/hooks/useMessages.ts:312) now writes optimism exclusively to the 
pending query, but [ChatWindow.tsx:76](E:/projects/virtual-office/src/components/messaging/ChatWindow.tsx:76) renders 
only stored pages. Holding creation before the server leaves its cleared input without a pending bubble. This affects 
the reachable debug comparison; the floor-plan entry currently has an empty People list. **Smallest fix:** make 
ChatWindow consume the existing merged message reader.

