   5: /**
   6:  * Phase 5 T25 — per-stream Realtime fault harness (SPEC §15, PLAN Standing
   7:  * rules: single-stream Phoenix frame shaping on the real socket).
   8:  *
   9:  * Makes ONE messaging Realtime stream of a browser context fail while every
  10:  * other channel on the same socket (the other messaging streams, Presence,
  11:  * Knock, spaces, …) keeps flowing untouched. The browser's own WebSocket to
  12:  * local Realtime stays the transport: `context.routeWebSocket` opens the
  13:  * server connection from the page with the native WebSocket and hands every
  14:  * frame to this module, which forwards it unchanged unless it belongs to the
  15:  * faulted stream. The app's joins, its realtime-js/Phoenix client, its
  16:  * subscribe callbacks and its retries are the real ones; no application
  17:  * health is set here.
  18:  *
  19:  * Streams (topic → stream; realtime-js prefixes every topic with `realtime:`):
  20:  *   messages  `messaging-db-changes:<companyId>:<userId>:<seq>:<uuid>`
  21:  *             (useMessageSubscription: messages, receipts, reactions; a new
  22:  *             topic on every application retry, so matched by prefix)
  23:  *   list      `conversations-changes` (useConversationRealtime)
  24:  *   typing    `conversation:<id>` (useConversationPresence, public, until T15)
  25:  *             or `conversation:<id>:typing` (T5 private topic, from T15)
  26:  *   presence  `company:<companyId>:presence` (observed only, never faulted)
  27:  *
  28:  * fail(stream, kind) — until restore(stream), every server frame of that
  29:  * stream is withheld (the stream is dark), and:
  30:  *   'error'   the current join gets a `phx_error` (Phoenix channel crash
  31:  *             signal; the client sees CHANNEL_ERROR and the SDK rejoins after
  32:  *             1/2/5/10 s); each later join attempt is forwarded to the server,
  33:  *             its real reply withheld and an error reply returned
  34:  *             (CHANNEL_ERROR again).
  35:  *   'timeout' the current join gets a `phx_error` (a joined channel cannot
  36:  *             time out: this makes the client rejoin, so the recorded sequence
  37:  *             starts CHANNEL_ERROR); each later join attempt is forwarded and
  38:  *             its reply withheld, so the client's own join timer (10 s) fires
  39:  *             TIMED_OUT.
  40:  *   'close'   REAL SERVER CLOSE: the harness sends, on the target topic only,
  41:  *             an `access_token` push with an invalid token; local Realtime
  42:  *             answers with its own `system` error and `phx_close` and ends the
  43:  *             server channel. The client sees CLOSED and, being closed rather
  44:  *             than errored, the SDK never rejoins it (terminal). A later join
  45:  *             attempt by the application is forwarded and its reply withheld
  46:  *             (TIMED_OUT), so the stream stays unavailable until restore.
  47:  * A fault armed while the stream has no joined channel only shapes its next
  48:  * joins (e.g. 'timeout' before a conversation is opened gives a pure TIMED_OUT).
  49:  *
  50:  * Statuses are read from the application's own subscribe callbacks: the
  51:  * messaging debug traces `[useMessageSubscription|useConversationRealtime|
  52:  * useConversationPresence:trace] status` (enabled by the `vo:debug:messaging`
  53:  * flag this harness sets) and Presence's `presence-observability-v1`
  54:  * subscription events.
  55:  *
  56:  * API (fixtures/messaging-phase5-faults.ts → `realtimeFaults.attach(device)`):
  57:  *   fail(stream, kind)          arm + kick; resolves with { mark, kicked }
  58:  *   restore(stream?)            stop shaping (all streams when omitted)
  59:  *   status(stream)              last status reported by the app callback
  60:  *   statuses(stream, {since})   status history ({ seq, at, status, … })
  61:  *   waitForStatus(stream, status, {since, timeout})
  62:  *   waitForReady(stream)        SUBSCRIBED, joined, and (postgres streams)
  63:  *                               server-confirmed changes stream
  64:  *   frames({stream, since, …})  frame log of the classified topics
  65:  *   mark()                      sequence point shared by frames and statuses
  66:  *   connections()               routed sockets (open/closed)
  67:  *   watchPage(page)             also record another tab's callbacks
  68:  *   redeliver(seq)              sends a passed server→page postgres_changes
  69:  *                               frame again, unchanged, on its socket (a
  70:  *                               duplicated delivery of a real frame)
