  12: /**
  13:  * Phase 5 T7 — client correlation by clientMessageId (FR-034, AC-050).
  14:  *
  15:  * A sends messages with IDENTICAL text — one plain, one replying to a message
  16:  * — while A has two tabs of the same session open on the conversation. Each
  17:  * message must show as exactly one bubble in both tabs throughout: no
  18:  * duplicate, no flash of two bubbles, no lost bubble, and the reply keeps its
  19:  * quoted parent.
  20:  *
  21:  * Ordering is produced by network shaping only: the create request reaches
  22:  * the real server (route.fetch), the real server stores the message and the
  23:  * real Realtime INSERT is published, and the HTTP response is held until the
  24:  * spec has seen that INSERT reach BOTH tabs' sockets (fault-harness frame
  25:  * log, passed frames only) and the stored bubble in both tabs; only then is
  26:  * the real response released (route.fulfill). The release time is compared
  27:  * with the frame times, so the order is proven, not assumed.
  28:  *
  29:  * "Throughout" is measured in the page: a MutationObserver re-counts the
  30:  * bubbles of each tracked message class (text + plain/reply) after every DOM
  31:  * change of each tab and keeps the maximum, whether a seen bubble ever
  32:  * disappeared, and whether a reply bubble ever lacked its parent quote.
  33:  *
  34:  *   1. one tab sends the plain message, then the reply (literal AC-050);
  35:  *   2. both messages are pending at once, one in each tab (the plain one's
  36:  *      request held before the server; the reply's INSERT reaches the plain
  37:  *      one's tab first): they must never be taken for each other;
  38:  *   3. the stored message reaches both tabs through a feed fetch, not
  39:  *      Realtime (the messages stream is faulted during the send; its
  40:  *      recovery catch-up refetches the feed) before the HTTP response: the
  41:  *      feed's own copy of the key must hide the pending one;
  42:  *   4. the stored message is deleted (A's own delete from another session,
  43:  *      through the Data API under RLS) after Realtime delivered it and before
  44:  *      its held HTTP response: it must never come back, as pending or stored,
  45:  *      in either tab;
  46:  *   5. a keyed message already loaded in an OLDER page is delivered again —
  47:  *      its real INSERT frame redelivered unchanged on the same channel, then
  48:  *      a refetch of every loaded page while newer messages shift the page
  49:  *      boundaries: one bubble, and no message id ever rendered twice.
  50:  */
