spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:45:## T8 — Durable outbox with ordered automatic delivery
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:47:Task: Every eligible text/reply send is written to a per-user 
IndexedDB outbox (key, conversation, content, reply target, requested mention IDs, original send time, window start, 
order, state, generation) before dispatch and before the composer clears; pending items render with a text label; 
items drain automatically per conversation in order when connectivity returns, with ≤ 10 pending and quota available 
all delivered within 10 s; confirmed items become the normal message; the outbox survives reload and tab close; 
attachments/voice are never queued (Phase 4 behavior kept); if the outbox write fails or storage is unavailable, 
nothing is dispatched and the text and reply stay with the D5 message.
