spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:74:Task: Definitive rejections show the item failed with its text 
and "Tentar de novo"/"Apagar" and block only later items of that conversation; "Apagar" removes it and the next item 
proceeds; 409 retry resends the content under a new key once; 429 and 401-with-valid-session stay pending and retry 
automatically in order; items fenced as not stored 24 h after send become "expirada" without auto-send (a fence 
answered 403 is a definitive failure, never "not stored" — T27); manual retry of an expired item keeps the key and the 
original send time and opens a new 24 h window under the normal rules.
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:81:## T11 — Identity fencing and session-end hold
spec-interview/phase-5-messaging-resilience/PLAN.md:83:Task: Before every dispatch and fence the authenticated 
application user must equal the item owner; an identity change or sign-out in any tab stops drains in all tabs; late 
create/fence/lookup responses after a switch, or older-generation/cancelled-item responses under the same identity, 
are discarded without changing any view, item, or claim; items are held only when the client auth state reports the 
session ended and drain after the same user signs in again; another user never sees, sends, or deletes them; a 401 
with a valid client session stays transient.
