I’m verifying that the buffer holds an unmutated reference to the original UTF-8 JSON string from the websocket, 
preserving byte accuracy without re-encoding. The redeliver method logs but doesn’t alter packets, so fail-open 
forwarding stays intact. This approach keeps memory usage low and supports reliable playback without raw byte mutation.
